Rebrand Mozilla CA store and organization references in certificate/MITM error pages and dialogs to Pyxis.

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
The unified diff below is generated from the checkout and is applied with
  git apply gecko/patches/pyxis/<path>.PYXIS_DIFF
(or `patch -p1 <`). Everything above this line is rationale, not content;
git apply ignores it. Regenerate with scripts/regen-gecko-patches.sh.
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

diff --git a/toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/neterror/certError.ftl b/toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/neterror/certError.ftl
index 76758fa314b8..dd425a853621 100644
--- a/toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/neterror/certError.ftl
+++ b/toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/neterror/certError.ftl
@@ -8,9 +8,9 @@ cert-error-intro = { $hostname } uses an invalid security certificate.
 
 cert-error-mitm-intro = Websites prove their identity via certificates, which are issued by certificate authorities.
 
-cert-error-mitm-mozilla = { -brand-short-name } is backed by the non-profit Mozilla, which administers a completely open certificate authority (CA) store. The CA store helps ensure that certificate authorities are following best practices for user security.
+cert-error-mitm-mozilla = { -brand-short-name } is backed by Pyxis, which administers an open certificate authority (CA) store. The CA store helps ensure that certificate authorities are following best practices for user security.
 
-cert-error-mitm-connection = { -brand-short-name } uses the Mozilla CA store to verify that a connection is secure, rather than certificates supplied by the user’s operating system. So, if an antivirus program or a network is intercepting a connection with a security certificate issued by a CA that is not in the Mozilla CA store, the connection is considered unsafe.
+cert-error-mitm-connection = { -brand-short-name } uses the Pyxis CA store to verify that a connection is secure, rather than certificates supplied by the user’s operating system. So, if an antivirus program or a network is intercepting a connection with a security certificate issued by a CA that is not in the Pyxis CA store, the connection is considered unsafe.
 
 cert-error-trust-unknown-issuer-intro = Someone could be trying to impersonate the site and you should not continue.
 
